## Impulsivity does not seem to be a behavioral trait {.center}


# Big team science


## What is big team science?

> Collaborations wherein a comparatively large number of researchers pool their intellectual and/or material resources to pursue a common goal

---Baumgartner et al., 2023 _Royal Society Open Science_.

::: {.fragment}
![](media/psa_map.png){fig-align="center" fig-alt="World map with pins showing locations of Psychological Science Accelerator research sites."}
:::

## Why big team science?

* Larger sample sizes
* Less effort per research site
* Consensus in methods design
* Diverse subject pool
* Many analysts involved in analysis
<!-- * Shared labor in data validation and code checking -->


## ManyDogs Project

International research consortium of scientists with shared interest in canine behavior and cognition

![](media/manydogs_banner.jpg){fig-align="center" height="300" fig-alt="ManyDogs logo"}


## ManyDogs Project Aims

::: {.incremental}
1. Attempt to replicate important studies
2. Investigate moderators that require large sample sizes
3. Develop consensus on methodological best practices
4. Investigate cultural differences
5. Set the bar for replicability of studies
:::


## ManyDogs 1

::: {.callout-tip}
## Research Question

::: {style="font-size: 40px"}
::: {.fragment}
Do dogs treat human pointing as communicative cues?
:::
:::
:::

::: {.fragment}
![](media/dog-pointing.jpg){fig-align="center" width="550" fig-alt="Black dog watching experimenter point to one of two blue cups."}
:::


## Results

::: {.r-stack}
![](media/md1_overall_accuracy_0.png){fig-align="center" height="550" fig-alt="Plot of Accuracy as a function of Condition (Non-communicative and Communicative). There are no data."}

![](media/md1_overall_accuracy_2.png){fig-align="center" height="550" .fragment fig-alt="Spaghetti plot of Accuracy as a function of Condition (Non-communicative and Communicative). Data show no discernable pattern."}

![](media/md1_overall_accuracy_4_last.png){fig-align="center" height="550" .fragment fig-alt="Spaghetti plot of Accuracy as a function of Condition (Non-communicative and Communicative) with group means and 95% confidence intervals overlaid. Means are slightly greater than chance (0.5) but not different from each other."}
:::

::: {.source}
[ManyDogs Project et al. 2023, _Animal Behavior & Cognition_](https://doi.org/10.26451/abc.10.03.03.2023)
:::


## Site effects

::: {.r-stack}
![](media/md1_site_accuracy_1.png){fig-align="center" height="550" fig-alt="Plot of Bias toward Communicative Accuracy for each Research site. There are no data."}

![](media/md1_site_accuracy_2_last.png){fig-align="center" height="550" .fragment fig-alt="Plot of Bias toward Communicative Accuracy for each Research site with each site's mean and 95% confidence intervale. Data show all but one site's confidence interval overlaps with 0, suggesting no difference between communicative and non-communicative conditions."}
:::

::: {.source}
[ManyDogs Project et al. 2023, _Animal Behavior & Cognition_](https://doi.org/10.26451/abc.10.03.03.2023)
:::


## Site differences

![](media/md1_owner_ages.png){fig-align="center" height="550" fig-alt="Panel of 17 histograms (one for each research site) showing frequency of participant owner ages across sites. Sites show marked variation with some uniformly distributed, some normally distributed, and some skewed to younger ages."}

::: {.source}
[ManyDogs Project et al. 2023, _Animal Behavior & Cognition_](https://doi.org/10.26451/abc.10.03.03.2023)
:::


## Study conclusions

::: {.incremental}
* Dogs were slightly better than chance but no difference between conditions

* Consistent findings across sites

* Results do not match robust literature showing point following

* Likely due to method choices

<!-- * Big differences in owner age distribution -->

:::


## Implications
::: {.incremental}
* Again, consider populations of owners and dogs
* Many analysts improved analysis
* Diverse viewpoints can bias methods
* Consider multi-site replication

:::


# Lessons Learned


## Reliable science

::: {.fragment}
![](media/replicable.jpeg){.absolute height=250 top="10%" left="5%" fig-alt="Illustration of two scientists replicating each other's chemistry experiment."}

